{"emerging_themes":[],"evidence_id":"0000093751_FY2024_item7_E03","motivation_status":"Explicit","motivations":[{"category_id":"M04","explanation":"The company states the MRM policy and framework are designed to monitor and control model risk, defined as adverse outcomes from incorrectly implemented or misused model outputs.","explicitness":"Explicit","quote":"Model risk is the potential for adverse outcomes due to incorrectly implemented or misused model outputs. Model Risk Management (MRM) is a separate control function within Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) responsible for specifying and maintaining the firmwide MRM policy and framework designed to monitor and control model risk within our risk appetite.","quote_locations":[{"end":222644,"start":222290}],"relationship_quote":"Model risk is the potential for adverse outcomes due to incorrectly implemented or misused model outputs. Model Risk Management (MRM) is a separate control function within Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) responsible for specifying and maintaining the firmwide MRM policy and framework designed to monitor and control model risk within our risk appetite.","relationship_quote_locations":[{"end":222644,"start":222290}]}],"practices":[{"category_id":"P03","explanation":"A model may not be used unless validation results or an MRC decision permit usage; linked context states AI/ML models are subject to this MRM regime.","quote":"Models used in the regulatory capital calculation can only be deployed for use after undergoing a model validation by ERM s MRM group. The model validation results and/or a decision by the MRC must permit model usage or the model may not be used.","quote_locations":[{"end":223829,"start":223583}]},{"category_id":"P04","explanation":"Concrete model validation and model-risk assessment standards are described within the MRM framework applicable to AI/ML models.","quote":"Model validation standards designed to verify that models are conceptually sound, are computationally accurate, are performing as expected, and are in line with their intended use, and evaluate the level of model risk for each model by considering the model s materiality, usage, performance, and sufficiency of compensating controls among other factors","quote_locations":[{"end":223497,"start":223144}]},{"category_id":"P05","explanation":"Explicit model risk management framework and policies apply to AI/ML models, requiring their compliance.","quote":"ERM s MRM group is responsible for defining the corporate-wide model risk management framework and maintaining policies that are designed to achieve the framework s objectives. All regulatory capital calculation models, including any artificial intelligence and machine learning models, must comply with the model risk management framework and corresponding policies.","quote_locations":[{"end":224199,"start":223832}]},{"category_id":"P09","explanation":"Ongoing model risk reporting, performance monitoring, and committee-level review are MRM responsibilities applicable to AI/ML models under the framework.","quote":"The group is responsible for overall model risk governance capabilities, with particular emphasis in the areas of model identification, model validation, model risk reporting, model performance monitoring, tracking of new model development status and committee-level review and challenge.","quote_locations":[{"end":224488,"start":224200}]}],"review_flag":false,"review_reason":"","uncodable":false,"vision_status":"Explicit","visions":[{"category_id":"V02","explanation":"The MRM framework’s validation standards aim to verify that models are sound, accurate, performing as expected, and aligned with intended use; AI/ML models must comply with this framework.","explicitness":"Explicit","quote":"Model validation standards designed to verify that models are conceptually sound, are computationally accurate, are performing as expected, and are in line with their intended use","quote_locations":[{"end":223323,"start":223144}],"relationship_quote":"The MRM framework includes: 
 Model risk governance that defines roles and responsibilities, including the authority to restrict model usage, provides policies and guidance, monitors compliance, and reports regularly to relevant internal committees and the Board of Directors on the overall degree of model risk across the firm; 
 Model development standards that focus on conceptual soundness and computational accuracy, data quality, robustness, stability, and sensitivity to assumptions; and 
 Model validation standards designed to verify that models are conceptually sound, are computationally accurate, are performing as expected, and are in line with their intended use","relationship_quote_locations":[{"end":223323,"start":222647}]}]}
